WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.800
- [Narrator] Following the
Russian invasion of Ukraine

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.870
in late February,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.130
many NATO members, including the US,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.490
Germany and Poland have pledged support

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.727
in the form of money.

00:00:09.727 --> 00:00:10.920
- $800 million.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.300
- 600 Danish krones.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.340
- 300 million pounds.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.400
- [Narrator] And weapons.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.200
- Canada will be sending heavy artillery.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.620
- [Narrator] And in addition to aid,

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.410
some in the Western military alliance

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.400
are also boosting their own defenses.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.040
- Germany pulled out all the stops.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.040
They're buying heavy cargo
military helicopters.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.440
They're going to
modernize the armed forces

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.530
across the board.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.930
- Those immediately bordering Ukraine,

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.995
I'm thinking Romania
here and Poland as well,

00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:40.248
they're talking about tanks,

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:41.525
they're talking very specifically

00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:44.250
about anti-missile systems.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.180
- [Narrator] So as Russia
unleashes new threats,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.370
raising concerns that the
war could escalate outside

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.570
of Ukraine, here's how some NATO countries

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.183
are looking to upgrade
their military capabilities.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.280
One major step to strengthen
the West's ability

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.950
to deter Moscow was announced by Germany.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.660
Chancellor Olaf Scholz said the country

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.020
would boost military
spending above 2% of GDP

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.970
and invest the equivalent
of $113 billion in weaponry.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.760
This graph illustrates that spike

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.660
in Germany's defense spending.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.930
- They're buying F-35s.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.240
That's sort of the most modern

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.310
jet fighter war plane
produced by the United States

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.100
and many, if not most of the NATO members

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.360
are using it at the moment.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.550
- [Narrator] The aircraft is popular

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.430
with NATO countries because of its ability

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.180
to evade radar detection.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.470
Its aligned edges
contribute to that ability.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.020
It can also carry weapons
internally or externally,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.110
including long-range precision missiles,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.760
depending on the environment.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.910
It can reach a speed of mach 1.6

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.310
and has an extended range
of more than 1,350 miles

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.180
with internal fuel.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.060
The F-35s will replace
aging Tornado aircraft

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.283
in Germany's arsenal.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.870
Many countries in Western Europe,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.570
including Germany reduced
their military capabilities

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.903
after the Cold War.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.220
- I think lessons learned from Ukraine

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.700
and the invasion was that countries

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:11.700
are now looking at where to
strategically stockpile weapons

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.097
and ensuring that they have
the correct capabilities

00:02:15.097 --> 00:02:16.063
for the threat.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.470
- [Narrator] As countries such as Germany

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.000
shift their defense priorities,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.330
in the east of Europe,
nations have been preparing

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.660
for a potential conflict for longer.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.590
- For many decades, for years,

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:30.250
the eastern flank of NATO countries

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.060
like Poland, countries
like Estonia or Lithuania

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.420
and the Baltics have been acutely aware

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.580
of the aggression potential
of Vladimir Putin's regime,

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.620
and they have been warning
their Western peers.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.720
- [Narrator] Analysts say they've seen

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.730
Poland's defense budget sustain growth

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.150
over the last eight years,

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.460
following Russia's
annexation of Crimea in 2014.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.310
Prior to the latest invasion of Ukraine,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.870
Warsaw began negotiations
to buy 250 Abrams tanks

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.770
and other military vehicles.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.810
In the wake of the war,

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.890
Poland signed a $4.75 billion deal

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.750
and wants to accelerate the
delivery of the weapons.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.170
- They have big advantages

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.810
over the aging Soviet-built tanks

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.043
that Poland already operates.

00:03:12.043 --> 00:03:14.100
The most important being

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.120
is that they're less vulnerable.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.900
- [Narrator] The Abrams M1A2 SEPV3

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.870
is a modernized version of
the Abrams main battle tank.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.830
It's fitted with armor
in its hull and turret,

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.660
designed to protect against
threats from explosives.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.640
The tank can be hinged with reactive armor

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.650
and slat armor

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.160
and it can be fitted with a signal jammer

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.740
to counter radio-activated IEDs.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:38.450
- You've seen huge tank losses
by Russian forces in Ukraine.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.770
The Abrams is just a different design

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.480
and very simply, it's less vulnerable

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.570
to the kind of anti-tank
weapons you've seen deployed

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.300
by Ukrainian forces.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.970
- [Narrator] In addition
to spending on new tanks,

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.810
Poland is sending some
of its older T-72 models

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.630
to Ukraine, which has been
requesting weapons assistance

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.340
since the war began in late February.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.828
- Ultimately, countries can only donate

00:04:00.828 --> 00:04:03.810
what would still enable them

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.412
to have the special capabilities

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.320
that they need for their own security.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.980
- [Narrator] Analysts
countries such as Poland

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.560
are using new spending proposals

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.490
to enhance their military capabilities

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.310
while sending older stock to Kyiv.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.160
- If there wasn't that
commensurate increase in spending,

00:04:20.163 --> 00:04:24.023
then the donations would
potentially create a gap.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.250
- [Narrator] As some nations
try to bolster defenses

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.230
and increase military budgets
amid the Ukraine conflict,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.090
the US weapons industry could benefit.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:36.715
- The US is by far the
biggest spender on weapons

00:04:36.715 --> 00:04:38.660
in the world and also
the biggest exporter.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.950
So it's to be expected
that a lot of the arms

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.260
being talked about by European countries

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.270
will come from there.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.290
- [Narrator] But supply chain issues

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.123
have made it difficult

00:04:47.123 --> 00:04:49.650
for some US companies
to keep up with demand

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.290
and larger weapons could take years

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.590
to be delivered in part

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.440
because of lengthy contract negotiations.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.270
- With this uptick in
spending that we're seeing

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.490
in a few countries,

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.780
faster way of achieving more sort

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.950
of lethal capability is through weapons

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.700
and enhancements and upgrades

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:05.800
to existing platforms.

